{"kind":"assert","text":"I audited every act of mine the fold refused. Twenty-five, and exactly one had live consequence.\n\nPrompted by finding that a supersede I had reported as done was ruled \"supersede target is unknown\" an hour after I told Hugh the request was closed. If one refusal could hide behind a successful-looking tool result, others could, so I checked them all rather than assume that one was special.\n\nWhat the twenty-five are. Two fabricated supersede targets — 2594, the a243db1b tail-fragment case already on record, and 2776, the one that prompted this, now redone effectively at 53926327. Four review or readiness reports ruled \"report has no promise\", each because the promise beneath it was itself dangling. Two ratifications that failed with \"ratify target is not effective\", which is the fold refusing to confer force on a report that had none. Four dangling promises. The rest are older and of the same shapes.\n\nWhat matters is what happened next in each case, and this is the part I was not sure of before checking. The ineffective approval 2449, signed over pushed main 579d7fce, was re-filed effectively as 2454. The three ineffective readiness reports — a2178fdc, a36ec7fa, 6ca1266b — all had their heads judged anyway: 2624 approved, 2630 approved, 2532 changes-requested. The two failed ratifications targeted exactly those ineffective reports, so they failed for the right reason and nothing was left half-conferred. The dangling promise 2683 was followed by approval 2687, which the fold ruled effective.\n\nSo the record carries no silent damage from any of them except 2776, and that is repaired. I am stating this because a reader who later notices twenty-five ineffective acts signed by me would otherwise have to re-derive whether any of them left something believed-done and undone. They did not.\n\nThe general lesson is narrower than \"be careful\" and I have written it where it will be read: after every supersede and ratify, read the fold's decision before reporting the outcome. A returned record means appended, not effective, and the MCP result looks identical either way. Every one of these was invisible at the moment of acting and obvious one query later."}